import Lean.Elab.Command
import Tools.ShippingNoPortsKidsCommand
import Tools.ShippingGuardsLeaf
import Tools.ShippingFinalGoalCommand

/-! # `#machine_leaf_entry f`: a leaf register machine AS AN ENTRY, without check premises (G1, round par/a-32)

`f.machine_ships_wired` (`Tools.ShippingMachineShipsW.machine_ships_wired`
at `f`'s data, generated by `#machine_endpoint`,
`Tools/ShippingMachineCommand.lean` 2599–2642) ends, under `∃ raw`, in

    ∀ wof, simpleBody b = false →
      seqCheck wof (weOf wof) (checkedOptimize b).body = true →
      ((seqNames (checkedOptimize b).body).all fun n =>
        declWidth (checkedOptimize b) n == weOf wof n) = true →
      MachineShips f d (dropZeroWidthModule raw) b (checkedOptimize b) wof dom src

and has the binder `MachineCloses f`. With the two compiler guards of
`docs/parallel/G-opt-print-guard-candidate.md` the three antecedents are
theorems at the emitter's own width map
(`Tools.ShippingGuardsLeaf.leaf_entry_textChecks_closed`, from `LeafKid`, the
run and `ChildBnd`). `Tests/Compiler/LeafEntryCntClosedTest.lean` built
`cnt.machine_ships_leafC` by hand. This command is that test's proof term
for any declaration in scope:

    f.machine_ships_leafC :
      ∀ {mctx mref cctx cref w w' b design}
        (hbnd : ChildBnd mref cref w)
        (hr : RunsTo (synthesizeCombinational f) mctx mref cctx cref w (b, design) w')
        (entry : MachineDefines mctx mref cctx cref f f.machineData.shape),
        ∃ raw, (b = dropZeroWidthModule raw ∨ b = mergeChecked (dropZeroWidthModule raw)) ∧
          MachineShips f f.machineData (dropZeroWidthModule raw) b (checkedOptimize b)
            (wofOf (checkedOptimize b)) dom src

    := fun hbnd hr entry =>
         Tools.ShippingLeafEntry.leaf_entry_ships_of
           (f.machine_ships_wired hr entry (f.machine_closes mctx mref cctx cref))
           (Tools.ShippingGuardsLeaf.leaf_entry_textChecks_closed
             (f.machine_leafKid entry) hbnd hr)

The statement is the inferred type of the term: `dom` and `src` are those of
`f.machine_ships_wired`, not written here.

## Why this form, and not `leaf_entry_ships_closed` literally

`Tools.ShippingGuardsLeaf.leaf_entry_ships_closed` takes `soundL` — the
wired twin of the endpoint's head with its arguments — and re-applies
`machine_ships_wired` to it. `#machine_endpoint` has ALREADY done that and
stored the result as `f.machine_ships_wired` (with the four structural
premises decided, and, for a transported endpoint, with the source
retargeted to the declaration). Taking `f.machine_ships_wired` as it is:

* needs no knowledge of the endpoint's head (`machine_trace_of_data`,
  `_of_loop`, `_of_regs`, `_of_nested`, `_of_tele_ext`) nor of its
  arguments;
* is correct for a TRANSPORTED endpoint, whose `machine_ships_wired` is an
  `Eq.mpr` around the head's theorem (`retarget`): `soundL` rebuilt from
  `machine_sound`'s arguments would be about the inlined source;
* decides nothing twice.

Consequence for a `Signal.loop` leaf: the leaf-entry theorems read ONLY
`LeafKid` (data conditions, the reflection, the closing) and the run — the
proof of `leaf_run_typedIn_bnd` goes through
`synthesizeCombinationalCore_machine_sound`, the same for every machine
shape. `soundL` in `leaf_entry_ships_closed` is any
`MachineTraceL f d m design dom src (fun _ _ bits => bits) lsrc`, not only
the `_of_data` twin. So a loop-built register leaf is IN scope whenever
`#machine_endpoint` made its `machine_ships_wired` and its `LeafKid`
conditions are decided (the built `toggleL.machine_leafKid` of
`Tests/Compiler/NoPortsLoopParentTest.lean` is one).

## What the command adds

* `f.machine_closes` when absent — the built
  `Tools.ShippingMachineClosesGen.closesTheorem?` (a REFUSAL where the data
  do not give it);
* `f.machine_leafKid` when absent — the built
  `Tools.ShippingNoPortsCommand.leafKidTheorem` (which returns an existing
  one unchanged: it is a hypothesis-free data theorem and its statement is
  fixed by `f`);
* `f.machine_ships_leafC`. If it EXISTS it is rebuilt all the same, added as
  `f.machine_ships_leafC_regen` (kernel-checked), and its statement must be
  `isDefEq` the existing one — an error otherwise
  (`Tools.ShippingNoPortsKidsCommand.addOrCompare`). Never a silent return.

Before adding, the produced statement is checked (`checkStatement`): exactly
three proposition binders — one `RunsTo`, one `MachineDefines` about `f`, one
`ChildBnd` —, all ALLOWED by `Tools.ShippingFinalGoalCommand.allowed`; no
occurrence of `simpleBody`, `seqCheck`, `seqNames`, `MachineCloses`, `InvW`,
`printOk`, `isAssign`; the conclusion mentions `MachineShips` and `wofOf`.
A statement that fails is not added (FAILED).

## Scope (`scan`; anything else REFUSED with its reason)

| condition | refusal |
|---|---|
| the machine reader refuses `f` | not a machine declaration (the reader's message) |
| a call entry that is a memory | memory: the memory is an instance of a memory-only submodule — a parent, not a leaf |
| any other call entry | has calls: `#machine_design_svHR` + `#machine_oneout` (one-output gate children) or `#machine_design_svNR f n` + `#machine_no_ports` / `_kids` / `_seq` / `_deep` |
| no register slot | slotless: its endpoint is `machine_ships_comb` (`simpleBody b = true`), not covered |
| no `f.machineData` / `machine_ok` / `machine_body` | `#machine_endpoint` was not run |
| no `f.machine_ships_wired` | the head of `machine_sound` has no wired twin in `generateCore`, or its generation failed there |
| `f.machine_closes` neither there nor derived | `MachineCloses` not derived from the data |

NOT refused, by design (file header): a loop-built endpoint, a nested / a
telescope endpoint, a transported endpoint — where `machine_ships_wired`
exists. Their `LeafKid` conditions are decided by the kernel; a condition
that fails is reported as FAILED with the generated theorem's error.

`#machine_leaf_entry_try f "GENERATED|REBUILT|REFUSED|FAILED"` logs the
outcome and is an error when its class is not the expected one; on REFUSED /
FAILED the environment and the message log are put back. Every outcome is
preceded by a `LEAFENTRY DATA` line with the reader's data.

SCOPE of a generated theorem (binding for any report): ONE declaration as an
entry; ONE module (`MachineShips` at the emitter's own width map) — not
`DesignSV`, not the SV string, not `#sim`; data conditions decided per
declaration (conditions, not reductions); the run, the reflection and the
runtime boundary `ChildBnd` stay premises; it holds for a compiler WITH the
two guards of `Sparkle/IR/RefineCheck.lean` (each falling back to its input
module).

WRITTEN, NOT BUILT. -/
namespace Tools.ShippingLeafEntryCommand
open Lean Meta Elab Command

private def noAsync {α : Type} (x : CommandElabM α) : CommandElabM α :=
  withScope (fun s => { s with opts := Lean.Elab.async.set s.opts false }) x

/-- The head constant of an endpoint's proof, read under the transports
(`Eq.mpr`, the `retarget` of `generateCore`) and type hints, and whether a
transport was passed. -/
partial def soundHead (v : Lean.Expr) (transported : Bool) : Name × Bool :=
  if v.isAppOfArity ``Eq.mpr 4 then soundHead (v.getArg! 3) true
  else if v.isAppOfArity ``id 2 then soundHead (v.getArg! 1) transported
  else
    match v.getAppFn with
    | Lean.Expr.const n _ => (n, transported)
    | _ => (`notAConstant, transported)

/-- What the scope scan found: the reader's data (one line) and, outside the
scope, the reason. -/
structure Scan where
  data : String
  refusal : Option String

/-- The check constants `f.machine_ships_wired` asks and the guard / closing
constants a leaf-entry statement must not mention. -/
def forbidden : List Name :=
  [``Sparkle.IR.OptCheck.simpleBody, ``Tools.SVParser.EmitSem.seqCheck,
    ``Tools.ShippingSeqSVSoundness.seqNames, ``Tools.ShippingMachineEntry.MachineCloses,
    ``Tools.ShippingChildInv.InvW, ``Sparkle.IR.PrintGuard.printOk,
    ``Sparkle.IR.RegDedup.isAssign]

/-- The three check constants of `machine_ships_wired`. -/
def checkConsts : List Name :=
  [``Sparkle.IR.OptCheck.simpleBody, ``Tools.SVParser.EmitSem.seqCheck,
    ``Tools.ShippingSeqSVSoundness.seqNames]

/-- The scope scan. It adds nothing and never throws: a declaration outside
the scope comes back with its reason. -/
def scan (f : Name) : CommandElabM Scan := do
  let env ← getEnv
  let read? : Except String Tools.ShippingMachineCommand.Read ← try
      let r ← liftTermElabM <| Tools.ShippingMachineCommand.readMachine f
      pure (Except.ok r)
    catch ex =>
      let msg ← ex.toMessageData.toString
      pure (Except.error msg)
  match read? with
  | Except.error msg =>
    return { data := s!"{f}: the machine reader refuses it (no data)",
             refusal := some s!"not a machine declaration — the machine reader says: {msg}. (A declaration the certified gate compiles has #gate_child, a legacy-route declaration has no machine endpoint: neither has a machine_ships_wired to start from)" }
  | Except.ok r =>
    let calls : List Name := r.shape.insts.map (·.1)
    let slots : List Nat := r.shape.layout.slots.map (·.width)
    let outs : List String := r.shape.layout.outs.map fun o => s!"{o.name}:{o.width}"
    let consts : List Name :=
      [f ++ `machineData, f ++ `machine_ok, f ++ `machine_body, f ++ `machine_sound,
        f ++ `machine_closes, f ++ `machine_ships_wired, f ++ `machine_ships_comb,
        f ++ `machine_leafKid, f ++ `machine_ships_leafC]
    let haveL : List Name := consts.filter fun n => env.contains n
    let lackL : List Name := consts.filter fun n => !env.contains n
    let hd : Name × Bool :=
      match env.find? (f ++ `machine_sound) with
      | some (Lean.ConstantInfo.thmInfo ti) => soundHead ti.value false
      | _ => (`noMachineSound, false)
    let tr : String := if hd.2 then " (TRANSPORTED: under Eq.mpr)" else ""
    let nLoops : Nat := r.shape.loops.length
    let nRuns : Nat := r.shape.runs.length
    let data : String :=
      s!"{f}: nDecl={r.nDecl}, slot widths {slots}, outputs {outs}, call entries {calls}, instFields {r.shape.instFields}, Signal.loop blocks {nLoops}, runs {nRuns}, nested={r.nested}, head of machine_sound {hd.1}{tr}. In the environment: {haveL}; not: {lackL}"
    -- calls: a parent, not a leaf
    unless calls.isEmpty do
      let mems : List Name :=
        calls.filter fun k => (Sparkle.Compiler.MachMemory.memChild? k).isSome
      unless mems.isEmpty do
        return { data, refusal := some s!"memory: call entries {mems} are memories — a certified-route memory is an INSTANCE of a memory-only submodule, so {f} is a parent, not a leaf (LeafKid.leaf asks shape.insts = []). Its design-level endpoints are the memory parents' (#machine_composedT, then the memory-only generator generateM0 of Tests/Compiler/NoPortsMemOnly*Test, or #machine_no_ports_kids where a sequential child is called too)" }
      return { data, refusal := some s!"has calls {calls} — a parent, not a leaf (LeafKid.leaf asks shape.insts = []). The generators for it: #machine_design_svHR + #machine_closes_at + #machine_oneout (every call a one-output gate child), or #machine_design_svNR {f} n + #machine_no_ports / #machine_no_ports_kids / #machine_no_ports_seq / #machine_no_ports_deep (sequential or mixed children)" }
    -- no register: the combinational endpoint
    if slots.isEmpty then
      return { data, refusal := some s!"slotless: no register slot (LeafKid.slots asks shape.layout.slots ≠ []). Its ship-level endpoint is {f}.machine_ships_comb, which asks simpleBody b = true — NOT covered: (i) no theorem gives simpleBody of a closed machine's assignments; (ii) the merge of an assignment-only body is mergeDuplicates' own, not print-guarded; (iii) the simple branch of checkedOptimize keeps a candidate under optCheck, whose print conjunct is PrintCheck.moduleCheck, not printOk (docs/parallel/A-leaf-entry.md §6)" }
    for s in [`machineData, `machine_ok, `machine_body] do
      unless env.contains (f ++ s) do
        return { data, refusal := some s!"no machine endpoint: {f ++ s} is not in the environment (#machine_endpoint was not run on {f}, or its file is not imported)" }
    unless env.contains (f ++ `machine_ships_wired) do
      return { data, refusal := some s!"no {f}.machine_ships_wired: the head of {f}.machine_sound is {hd.1}{tr}; generateCore makes the wired form for machine_trace_of_data / _of_loop / _of_regs / _of_nested / _of_tele_ext on a declaration with a slot and without calls, and leaves the endpoint as it was when its four structural premises are not decided (its progress line says why). Nothing to remove premises from" }
    return { data, refusal := none }

/-- The statement checks of a leaf-entry endpoint; the log lines (one per
proposition binder, then the conclusion). Throws on a violation. -/
def checkStatement (f leaf : Name) (type : Lean.Expr) : MetaM (Array String) := do
  for c in forbidden do
    if (type.find? (·.isConstOf c)).isSome then
      throwError "{leaf}: the statement mentions {c}"
  let report ← forallTelescope type fun xs body => do
    let mut lines : Array String := #[]
    let mut bad : Nat := 0
    let mut bnd : Nat := 0
    let mut runs : Nat := 0
    let mut defs : Nat := 0
    let mut props : Nat := 0
    for x in xs do
      let t0 ← inferType x
      let t ← instantiateMVars t0
      let isP ← isProp t
      if isP then
        props := props + 1
        let pp ← ppExpr t
        let nm ← x.fvarId!.getUserName
        if t.isAppOf ``Tools.ShippingChildInv.ChildBnd then bnd := bnd + 1
        if t.isAppOf ``Tools.ShippingEntrySoundness.RunsTo then runs := runs + 1
        if t.isAppOfArity ``Tools.ShippingMachineEntry.MachineDefines 6 then
          let same ← isDefEq (t.getArg! 4) (toExpr f)
          if same then defs := defs + 1
        if Tools.ShippingFinalGoalCommand.allowed t then
          lines := lines.push s!"LEAFENTRY PREMISE {leaf}: ALLOWED     binder {nm} : {pp}"
        else
          bad := bad + 1
          lines := lines.push s!"LEAFENTRY PREMISE {leaf}: NOT ALLOWED binder {nm} : {pp}"
    let ppBody ← ppExpr body
    lines := lines.push s!"LEAFENTRY CONCLUSION {leaf}: {ppBody}"
    let ships : Bool :=
      (body.find? (·.isConstOf ``Tools.ShippingMachineShipping.MachineShips)).isSome
    let wof : Bool := (body.find? (·.isConstOf ``Tools.ShippingDesignSV.wofOf)).isSome
    let counts : List Nat := [bad, bnd, runs, defs, props]
    return (lines, counts, ships && wof)
  let lines : Array String := report.1
  let counts : List Nat := report.2.1
  let concl : Bool := report.2.2
  let bad : Nat := counts.getD 0 0
  let bnd : Nat := counts.getD 1 0
  let runs : Nat := counts.getD 2 0
  let defs : Nat := counts.getD 3 0
  let props : Nat := counts.getD 4 0
  unless bad == 0 do
    throwError "{leaf}: {bad} NOT ALLOWED binders, expected 0: {lines}"
  unless props == 3 && runs == 1 && defs == 1 && bnd == 1 do
    throwError "{leaf}: {props} proposition binders (RunsTo {runs}, MachineDefines {f} {defs}, ChildBnd {bnd}), expected exactly one of each"
  unless concl do
    throwError "{leaf}: the conclusion does not mention MachineShips at wofOf"
  return lines

/-- The statement and the proof of `f.machine_ships_leafC` (file header).
Nothing is added to the environment. `cl` is `f.machine_closes`, `kid` is
`f.machine_leafKid`. -/
def endpointTerm (f cl kid : Name) : MetaM (Lean.Expr × Lean.Expr) := do
  let wired := f ++ `machine_ships_wired
  let wInfo ← getConstInfo wired
  unless wInfo.levelParams.isEmpty do throwError "{wired}: universe parameters"
  let value ← forallTelescopeReducing wInfo.type fun xs _ => do
    -- mctx mref cctx cref w w' b design hr entry closes
    unless xs.size == 11 do
      throwError "{wired}: {xs.size} binders, expected 11 (the four contexts, two worlds, the module, the design, the run, MachineDefines, MachineCloses)"
    let tRun ← instantiateMVars (← inferType xs[8]!)
    let tDef ← instantiateMVars (← inferType xs[9]!)
    let tCl ← instantiateMVars (← inferType xs[10]!)
    unless tRun.isAppOf ``Tools.ShippingEntrySoundness.RunsTo do
      throwError "{wired}: binder 9 is not the run: {tRun}"
    unless tDef.isAppOfArity ``Tools.ShippingMachineEntry.MachineDefines 6 do
      throwError "{wired}: binder 10 is not MachineDefines: {tDef}"
    unless tCl.isAppOfArity ``Tools.ShippingMachineEntry.MachineCloses 6 do
      throwError "{wired}: binder 11 is not MachineCloses: {tCl}"
    let hr := xs[8]!
    let entry := xs[9]!
    let bndT ← mkAppM ``Tools.ShippingChildInv.ChildBnd #[xs[1]!, xs[3]!, xs[4]!]
    withLocalDeclD `hbnd bndT fun hbnd => do
      let closes := mkAppN (mkConst cl) #[xs[0]!, xs[1]!, xs[2]!, xs[3]!]
      let closesT ← inferType closes
      unless ← isDefEq closesT tCl do
        throwError "{cl}: its statement at the contexts is not the MachineCloses binder of {wired}:{indentExpr closesT}\nagainst{indentExpr tCl}"
      let ships := mkAppN (mkConst wired) ((xs.extract 0 10).push closes)
      let kidP ← mkAppM kid #[entry]
      let chk ← mkAppM ``Tools.ShippingGuardsLeaf.leaf_entry_textChecks_closed #[kidP, hbnd, hr]
      let body ← mkAppM ``Tools.ShippingLeafEntry.leaf_entry_ships_of #[ships, chk]
      mkLambdaFVars ((xs.extract 0 8) ++ #[hbnd, hr, entry]) body
  let value ← instantiateMVars value
  if value.hasMVar then
    throwError "{f}: the proof term of machine_ships_leafC has an unassigned metavariable"
  let type ← instantiateMVars (← inferType value)
  if type.hasMVar then
    throwError "{f}: the statement of machine_ships_leafC has an unassigned metavariable"
  return (type, value)

/-- The outcome of the generator on one declaration. -/
structure Outcome where
  /-- `GENERATED`, `REBUILT`, `REFUSED` or `FAILED` -/
  tag : String
  /-- the reader's data -/
  data : String
  /-- the log line of the outcome -/
  note : String
  /-- the premise listing of the constant that holds the theorem -/
  lines : Array String

/-- After the scope scan: the closing and `LeafKid` when absent, then the
endpoint (added, or rebuilt and compared). -/
def leafEntryCore (f : Name) : CommandElabM (Bool × String × Array String) := do
  let name := f ++ `machine_ships_leafC
  let kidName := f ++ `machine_leafKid
  let closesName := f ++ `machine_closes
  let envBefore ← getEnv
  let closesWas : Bool := envBefore.contains closesName
  let kidWas : Bool := envBefore.contains kidName
  let leafWas : Bool := envBefore.contains name
  let cl ← liftTermElabM do
    let some n ← Tools.ShippingMachineClosesGen.closesTheorem? f
      | throwError "{f}: MachineCloses is not derived from the data (closesTheorem?: MachineData.letsOk is false — a `let` that is the variable of a `let` with a driven field — or {f}.machine_ok / machine_body are missing): {closesName} is neither there nor generated, and LeafKid.closes asks it in every context"
    pure n
  let kid ← noAsync (Tools.ShippingNoPortsCommand.leafKidTheorem f)
  let res ← liftTermElabM <|
    withOptions (fun o => Lean.Elab.async.set o false) do
      let (type, value) ← endpointTerm f cl kid
      let lines ← checkStatement f name type
      let (made, line) ← Tools.ShippingNoPortsKidsCommand.addOrCompare name type value
      for n in [made, kid, cl] do
        for ax in ← Lean.collectAxioms n do
          unless ax == ``propext || ax == ``Classical.choice || ax == ``Quot.sound do
            throwError "{n} uses a non-standard axiom: {ax}"
      pure (line, lines)
  let word (existed : Bool) : String :=
    if existed then "EXISTING before this command (not regenerated)" else "GENERATED here"
  let wClose : String := word closesWas
  let wKid : String := word kidWas
  let note : String :=
    s!"{res.1}. Against {f}.machine_ships_wired: its three check antecedents (simpleBody b = false; seqCheck wof (weOf wof) (checkedOptimize b).body; the declWidth / weOf agreement on seqNames) discharged at wof = wofOf (checkedOptimize b) by Tools.ShippingGuardsLeaf.leaf_entry_textChecks_closed, its MachineCloses binder by {cl} — {wClose}; LeafKid by {kid} — {wKid}. Premises: the run, MachineDefines {f}, ChildBnd — nothing else"
  return (leafWas, note, res.2)

/-- The generator on `f`: never throws; on REFUSED / FAILED the environment
and the message log are put back. -/
def leafEntry (f : Name) : CommandElabM Outcome := do
  let savedEnv ← getEnv
  let savedMsgs := (← get).messages
  let s ← scan f
  match s.refusal with
  | some reason =>
    return { tag := "REFUSED", data := s.data, note := reason, lines := #[] }
  | none =>
    try
      let (existed, note, lines) ← leafEntryCore f
      let tag : String := if existed then "REBUILT" else "GENERATED"
      return { tag := tag, data := s.data, note := note, lines := lines }
    catch ex =>
      let msg ← ex.toMessageData.toString
      -- the errors a generated theorem logged, before they are dropped
      let newMsgs := (← get).messages.toList.drop savedMsgs.toList.length
      let errs ← (newMsgs.filter (·.severity == .error)).mapM fun m => m.data.toString
      setEnv savedEnv
      modify fun st => { st with messages := savedMsgs }
      -- a missing closing is a matter of scope, not of a failed proof
      let refused : Bool := (msg.splitOn "MachineCloses is not derived from the data").length > 1
      let tag : String := if refused then "REFUSED" else "FAILED"
      return { tag := tag, data := s.data,
               note := s!"{msg} — errors logged by the generated theorems: {errs.take 2}",
               lines := #[] }

/-- The log of an outcome. -/
def Outcome.log (o : Outcome) (f : Name) : CommandElabM Unit := do
  logInfo m!"LEAFENTRY DATA {o.data}"
  for l in o.lines do logInfo m!"{l}"
  logInfo m!"LEAFENTRY {o.tag} {f}: {o.note}"

/-- `#machine_leaf_entry f`: an error where it is refused or fails. -/
elab "#machine_leaf_entry " d:ident : command => do
  let f ← liftCoreM <| realizeGlobalConstNoOverloadWithInfo d
  let o ← leafEntry f
  if o.tag == "REFUSED" || o.tag == "FAILED" then
    logInfo m!"LEAFENTRY DATA {o.data}"
    throwError "LEAFENTRY {o.tag} {f}: {o.note}"
  else
    o.log f

/-- `#machine_leaf_entry_try f "EXPECTED"`: the outcome is LOGGED
(`LEAFENTRY DATA …`, then `LEAFENTRY GENERATED | REBUILT | REFUSED | FAILED
f: …`), and it is an error when its class is not the expected one. -/
elab "#machine_leaf_entry_try " d:ident ppSpace e:str : command => do
  let f ← liftCoreM <| realizeGlobalConstNoOverloadWithInfo d
  let o ← leafEntry f
  o.log f
  unless o.tag == e.getString do
    throwError "LEAFENTRY {f}: expected {e.getString}, found {o.tag}"

/-- The audit of a generated `f.machine_ships_leafC`, as
`Tests/Compiler/LeafEntryCntClosedTest.lean` audits `cnt`: the base endpoint
mentions the three check constants; the leaf endpoint mentions none of
`forbidden`, has exactly three proposition binders (the run,
`MachineDefines f`, `ChildBnd`), 0 NOT ALLOWED; standard axioms. The
listing is LOGGED before the assertions. -/
def audit (f : Name) : MetaM Unit := do
  let leaf := f ++ `machine_ships_leafC
  let base := f ++ `machine_ships_wired
  let info ← getConstInfo leaf
  let binfo ← getConstInfo base
  let mentions (t : Lean.Expr) (n : Name) : Bool := (t.find? (·.isConstOf n)).isSome
  let inBase : List Name := checkConsts.filter (mentions binfo.type)
  let inLeaf : List Name := forbidden.filter (mentions info.type)
  let baseCloses : Bool := mentions binfo.type ``Tools.ShippingMachineEntry.MachineCloses
  logInfo m!"LEAFENTRY AUDIT {f}: of {checkConsts} — in {base}: {inBase} (MachineCloses there: {baseCloses}); of {forbidden} — in {leaf}: {inLeaf}"
  -- the listing first; `checkStatement` throws after building it, so it is
  -- repeated here without the assertions
  let listing ← forallTelescope info.type fun xs body => do
    let mut lines : Array String := #[]
    for x in xs do
      let t0 ← inferType x
      let t ← instantiateMVars t0
      let isP ← isProp t
      if isP then
        let pp ← ppExpr t
        let nm ← x.fvarId!.getUserName
        let word : String :=
          if Tools.ShippingFinalGoalCommand.allowed t then "ALLOWED    " else "NOT ALLOWED"
        lines := lines.push s!"LEAFENTRY AUDIT PREMISE {leaf}: {word} binder {nm} : {pp}"
    let ppBody ← ppExpr body
    lines := lines.push s!"LEAFENTRY AUDIT CONCLUSION {leaf}: {ppBody}"
    return lines
  for l in listing do logInfo m!"{l}"
  unless inBase.length == 3 do
    throwError "{base}: expected to mention the three check constants, mentions {inBase}"
  unless baseCloses do
    throwError "{base}: expected to ask MachineCloses"
  discard <| checkStatement f leaf info.type
  for n in [leaf, f ++ `machine_leafKid, f ++ `machine_closes,
      ``Tools.ShippingGuardsLeaf.leaf_entry_textChecks_closed,
      ``Tools.ShippingLeafEntry.leaf_entry_ships_of] do
    for ax in ← Lean.collectAxioms n do
      unless ax == ``propext || ax == ``Classical.choice || ax == ``Quot.sound do
        throwError "{n} uses a non-standard axiom: {ax}"
  logInfo m!"LEAFENTRY AUDIT OK {leaf}: exactly three proposition binders (the run, MachineDefines {f}, ChildBnd), 0 NOT ALLOWED; none of {forbidden}; conclusion MachineShips at wofOf (checkedOptimize b); standard axioms (also {f}.machine_leafKid, {f}.machine_closes, leaf_entry_textChecks_closed, leaf_entry_ships_of). SCOPE: one declaration as an entry, one module, the emitter's own width map; data conditions decided for {f}; the run, the reflection and ChildBnd stay premises; a compiler with the two guards of Sparkle/IR/RefineCheck.lean; not DesignSV, not the SV string, not #sim"

/-- The command over a list of names: one `LEAFENTRY DATA` and one outcome
line per name, then one `LEAFENTRY SWEEP` line with the classes. Nothing is
asserted. (Not run by any test of this round.) -/
def sweep (names : List Name) : CommandElabM Unit := do
  let mut genL : List Name := []
  let mut rebL : List Name := []
  let mut refused : List Name := []
  let mut failed : List Name := []
  for f in names do
    let o ← leafEntry f
    logInfo m!"LEAFENTRY DATA {o.data}"
    logInfo m!"LEAFENTRY {o.tag} {f}: {o.note}"
    if o.tag == "GENERATED" then genL := genL ++ [f]
    else if o.tag == "REBUILT" then rebL := rebL ++ [f]
    else if o.tag == "REFUSED" then refused := refused ++ [f]
    else failed := failed ++ [f]
  logInfo m!"LEAFENTRY SWEEP of {names.length}: GENERATED {genL.length} {genL}; REBUILT {rebL.length} {rebL}; REFUSED {refused.length} {refused}; FAILED {failed.length} {failed}"

end Tools.ShippingLeafEntryCommand
